---
import AppLayout from '../layouts/AppLayout.astro';
---
<AppLayout title="Reference Sheet">
  <section class="page-width page-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Notation & formulas · quick reference</p>
    <h1 class="display-title">A map of the symbols, not a substitute for the reasoning.</h1>
    <p class="lede">Use this sheet after you understand the model. Every formula points back to a live lab where the assumptions, representation, and steps are visible.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-width reference-grid" aria-label="AMAT 19 formula and notation reference">
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Logic</p><h2>Connectives</h2><dl><div><dt>∼P</dt><dd>negation · flips the truth value</dd></div><div><dt>P ∧ Q</dt><dd>conjunction · true only when both are true</dd></div><div><dt>P ∨ Q</dt><dd>inclusive disjunction · false only when both are false</dd></div><div><dt>P → Q</dt><dd>implication · false only when P is true and Q is false</dd></div><div><dt>P ↔ Q</dt><dd>biconditional · true when P and Q agree</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/truth-table">Open Truth Table Lab →</a></article>
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Probability</p><h2>Counting & conditioning</h2><dl><div><dt>P(n,r)=n!/(n-r)!</dt><dd>ordered selection without repetition</dd></div><div><dt>C(n,r)=n!/[r!(n-r)!]</dt><dd>unordered selection without repetition</dd></div><div><dt>|A∪B|=|A|+|B|−|A∩B|</dt><dd>two-set inclusion–exclusion</dd></div><div><dt>P(A|B)=P(A∩B)/P(B)</dt><dd>condition on B; the denominator becomes B</dd></div><div><dt>P(A∩B)=P(A)P(B)</dt><dd>exact independence test</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/conditional-probability">Open Probability Lab →</a></article>
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Financial Mathematics</p><h2>Move values through time</h2><dl><div><dt>A=P(1+it)</dt><dd>simple interest</dd></div><div><dt>A=P(1+i)^t</dt><dd>compound interest with one effective rate per period</dd></div><div><dt>A=P(1+j/m)<sup>mt</sup></dt><dd>nominal annual rate j convertible m times per year</dd></div><div><dt>i=(1+j/m)^m−1</dt><dd>equivalent annual effective rate</dd></div><div><dt>v<sup>n</sup>=(1+i)<sup>−n</sup></dt><dd>discount n periods to the focal date</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/interest">Open Interest & TVM Lab →</a></article>
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Matrices</p><h2>Compatibility & row operations</h2><dl><div><dt>A+B</dt><dd>requires equal dimensions</dd></div><div><dt>AB</dt><dd>requires columns(A)=rows(B)</dd></div><div><dt>(AB)ᵢⱼ</dt><dd>row i of A dotted with column j of B</dd></div><div><dt>[A|I] → [I|A⁻¹]</dt><dd>Gauss–Jordan inverse when the left block can become I</dd></div><div><dt>RREF([A|b])</dt><dd>reveals unique, infinite, or inconsistent systems</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/row-reduction">Open Gauss–Jordan Lab →</a></article>
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Linear Programming</p><h2>Feasible first, optimize second</h2><dl><div><dt>ax+by≤c</dt><dd>one half-plane constraint</dd></div><div><dt>Z=c₁x+c₂y</dt><dd>linear objective</dd></div><div><dt>corner-point principle</dt><dd>a bounded 2D LP reaches an optimum at a feasible vertex; an entire edge may also be optimal</dd></div><div><dt>unbounded</dt><dd>a feasible recession direction improves Z indefinitely</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/linear-programming">Open LP Lab →</a></article>
    <article class="reference-section"><p class="eyebrow">Game Theory</p><h2>Zero-sum security levels</h2><dl><div><dt>maximin</dt><dd>row player chooses the row with the largest row minimum</dd></div><div><dt>minimax</dt><dd>column player chooses the column with the smallest column maximum</dd></div><div><dt>maximin=minimax</dt><dd>a pure saddle point exists</dd></div><div><dt>mixed strategy</dt><dd>when no pure saddle exists, probabilities can make the opponent indifferent in supported 2×2 games</dd></div></dl><a class="text-link" href="/labs/game-theory">Open Game Theory Lab →</a></article>
  </section>
</AppLayout>
